//! Shared normalization of Kio'-shaped terms under explicit pure primitives.
//!
//! Equivalence checks, REPL expression queries, in-memory source normalization,
//! and user elaborators share this reduction engine and residual value domain.
//!
//! The evaluator walks typed `Expr<UncheckedPrime>` terms in an environment
//! of parameter bindings and reduces them to a [`Value`] — a small ADT
//! covering closed values (units, literals, closures), free variables
//! (parameter references, host items, unresolvable names), and stuck
//! applications (a function position that cannot be reduced).
//!
//! ## Phase boundary
//!
//! Public callers consume boundary-local elaborations before constructing an
//! [`EvalArtifact`]. The reducer and its compiled-function cache receive only
//! that self-contained Kio'-shaped artifact plus its explicit primitive
//! environment; no elaboration table or ambient producer provenance is
//! available during reduction. The compiled evaluator representation retains
//! the nominal artifact generation, resolved module, and exact retained node
//! of each structural-recursion helper occurrence as explicit, phase-local
//! totality state.
//!
//! `kio test` invokes the evaluator on every arm body of every
//! `equiv` decl in a typed module and compares the resulting [`Value`]
//! trees up to alpha- and eta-equivalence. The arms pass when their
//! NFs are equal.
//!
//! Host items (host `fn`s, host types, host literals) flow through
//! as opaque [`Value::Atom`]s with the dotted reference as the atom's
//! identity. Anything the evaluator cannot reduce — pattern matches
//! against host atoms, intrinsic-style applications without an
//! elaboration entry — also residualizes structurally so two such
//! sites with the same shape compare equal.
//!
//! ## Coverage
//!
//! The evaluator is complete with respect to the reduction relation
//! and equivalence in [`specs/formal/equiv.md`]; a `Value::Atom` /
//! `Value::Stuck` / `Value::Seq` residual is admissible only for a genuinely
//! irreducible term (matching the § 3 residual-NF grammar), never to
//! paper over a missing rule.
//!
//! Reduces:
//!
//! - Lambda introduction (`fn`) and application (β-reduction); `let`
//!   blocks; and pure `(); rest` sequence collapse. A sequence whose
//!   left side is a stuck unit-typed host action stays residual.
//! - **Type application / Λ (§ 1, prime.md § 3 β-TLam).** Type
//!   parameters are erased: a polymorphic `fn`'s type binders carry no
//!   runtime value, so applying it drops the type-args and β-reduces
//!   the value layer through. Kio' has no anonymous type-level
//!   abstraction, so there is no separate `Λ` value to reduce —
//!   erasure *is* β-TLam here.
//! - `Path` references against the local env, falling back to a
//!   pure-fn unfold for any `fn` reachable in the current module:
//!   same-module declarations, selective `import other/module(a, b);`
//!   imports (single-segment), and `import other as alias;` qualified
//!   imports (`alias.foo`, two-segment).
//! - The ordinary Kio' forms produced by lowering surface `match!`, `if`/`else`,
//!   and elaborator calls before this evaluator is entered.
//! - **Constructors build [`Value::Data`]** — `__left__` /
//!   `__right__` / `__pair__` and every newtype constructor
//!   `N.c` genuinely construct, dropping their leading erased type-args.
//! - **Eliminators case-reduce over [`Value::Data`]** — the ι-rules of
//!   § 2.1: ι-LeftEither / ι-RightEither (`__either__`), ι-Fst / ι-Snd
//!   (`__fst__` / `__snd__`), ι-Newtype (`N.p(N.c(v)) → v`), and ι-If
//!   (`__if_then_else__` over a literal `.t` / `.f`, § 2.2).
//! - **Symbolic case-split over an opaque sum (§ 2.6)** — `__either__`
//!   over an `equiv` sum-typed parameter (or any non-injection
//!   residual) residualizes to a [`Value::CaseSplit`], applying each
//!   handler to a fresh per-branch payload atom; nested `__either__`
//!   distributes over an inner case-split.
//! - **η laws (§ 4.2)** in [`nf_eq`]: function η (`λx. f(x) ≃ f`),
//!   product η (`__pair__(__fst__(p), __snd__(p)) ≃ p`), and sum η
//!   (`__either__(s, __left__, __right__) ≃ s`, over a
//!   case-split).
//! - Tuple, fn-placeholder, and label-value: statically uninhabited in Kio'.
//!
//! Stays as a residual (the § 3 residual-NF grammar, genuine opacity):
//!
//! - Free atoms — `equiv` parameters, unbound names, and host items
//!   (host `fn`s / types / literals, reached as multi-segment paths) —
//!   return a [`Value::Atom`] keyed by the dotted name.
//! - Host calls and other applications whose callee is unreducible
//!   (an atom or another stuck value), and eliminators whose scrutinee
//!   is opaque and not a sum (`__fst__` / `__snd__` / `N.p` /
//!   `__if_then_else__` over a stuck residual) — return a
//!   [`Value::Stuck`] carrying the callee and the reduced args.
//!   `__absurd__` has no reduction rule (§ 2.3) and stays stuck.
//! - Sequence statements whose discarded value is a stuck unit-typed
//!   residual — return a [`Value::Seq`] carrying the discarded action
//!   and the reduced body.

